<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s230S">The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w1">Sixty Verses on <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s230m2">Reasoning</span></span> say <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p3">as well</span>, The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w4">world</span> is something that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w5">ignorance</span> causes; Why? <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w8">For</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w9">Buddhas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w10">say</span> it is so. And <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p17">why</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w11">then</span> would it be <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w18">wrong</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p16">to say</span> That <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w13">this</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w12">world</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p15">is</span> only <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w14">conceptions</span>. The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w19">meaning</span> of this verse, according to the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w20">commentary</span>, is that <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p26">none</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w21">many <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s230m22">worlds</span></span> that exist <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w27">does so</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w23">through some <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s230m24">essence</span> of its own</span>: none of them are anything more than <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w29">products</span> of our <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w28">conception</span>.</span>
</div>
